{{Quote|Watch out! Wisties!|An Imperial stormtrooper|audio=WatchOutWisties.flac|<ref name="BF II" />}}
'''Wisties''', also known as '''fire sprites''' or '''firefolk''', were a small, [[Bioluminescence|radiant]], [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] native to the [[Endor|Forest Moon of Endor]]. Like the [[Ewok]]s, with whom they shared their [[homeworld]], the [[fairy]]-like flying Wisties were fierce defenders of their [[forest]]s, and the two species were allies. Ewoks sometimes used pouches full of Wisties as a weapon against intruders, such as [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[stormtrooper]]s. They threw the pouches in the direction of a target; on impact, the sprites emerged and attacked the invaders.

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|Firefolk! Get away from them!|An Imperial stormtrooper, under attack by Wisties emerged from an Ewok's pouch|audio=FirefolkGetAwayFromThem.flac|<ref name="BF II" />}}
[[File:WistiesOnEndor-TalesFromVadersCastle4.jpg|thumb|right|250px|A pair of Wisties]]
Wisties, also referred to as fire sprites or firefolk, were a tiny,<ref name="BF II" /> [[Color|orange]]-skinned,<ref name="TfVC 4" /> [[fairy]]-like,<ref name="BMF 38">{{BuildFalconCite|38|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] native to the [[Endor|Forest Moon of Endor]]. Bearing resemblance to a [[human]] sillouette,<ref name="SWE" /> the unique creatures<ref name="BMF 38" /> possessed a head, torso, two [[Limb|legs]], and two arms, with the latter ending in three-fingered hands.<ref name="BF II" /> While the [[Bioluminescence|phosphorescent]] fire sprites were the size of a [[bat]], they appeared as moving [[Fire|flames]]. Their wings enabled them to fly,<ref name="SWE" /> which they did while making buzzing, squeaking sounds.<ref name="BF II" />

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|Fire sprites incoming!|An Imperial stormtrooper being burned by Wisties|audio=FirespritesIncoming.flac|<ref name="BF II" />}}
Maintaining good relations with the [[Ewok]]s,<ref name="SWE" /> Wisties lived in the Endor [[forest]]s and were fierce defenders of their home. They were capable of burning enemies by touching them.<ref name="BF II" />

==History==
===Wearisome weapons===
{{Quote|Gah! ''Get away, will you! Shoo. Shoo.''&raquo;<br />&laquo;''What are you ''doing'', Chirpa? Stop fooling around.''&raquo;<br />&laquo;''It's these stupid Wisties. Makrit should do something about them.''|translated=1|italics=0|Chirpa and Ra-Lee, in Ewokese|<ref name="TfVC 4" />}}
[[File:Ewok_Wistie.png|thumb|left|275px|Ewoks used pouches full of Wisties as a weapon against invaders.]]
In the [[Standard year|year]] [[1 BBY]],<ref name="TfVC 4 date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars Adventures: Tales from Vader's Castle 4|''Star Wars Adventures: Tales from Vader's Castle'' 4]] that take place on the [[Endor|Forest Moon of Endor]] to [[1 BBY]].</ref> the Ewoks [[Chirpa]] and [[Ra-Lee]] went [[hunting]] [[Boar-wolf|boar-wolves]] in the Endor forests. During the hunt, Chirpa was annoyed by a pair of Wisties flying around him. Viewing them as a nuisance, he shooed the Wisties away and stated that [[Makrit]], [[shaman]] of their [[Bright Tree tribe|Ewok tribe]], should do something about the creatures.<ref name="TfVC 4" />

When the Forest [[Moon]] was later [[Occupation of Endor|occupied]] by the [[Galactic Empire]] during the [[Battle of Endor]]<ref name="BF II" /> in [[4 ABY]],<ref name="SWT">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> Wisties and Ewoks joined forces to defend their shared [[homeworld]] against Imperial [[stormtrooper]]s. In battle, Ewoks sometimes used [[Wistie capsule|pouches]] full of Wisties as a weapon, throwing them in the direction of a target. Upon impact, the sprites emerged as swarms, both disrupting and burning the target.<ref name="BF II" /> Wisties were also the subject of the term "Wistie tale," which referred to a made-up story. As a young Ewok, [[Wicket Wystri Warrick]] believed that the legendary creature [[Kroolok]] was a Wistie tale fabricated to scare [[wokling]]s.<ref name="Kroolok">{{StoryCite|story=The Kroolok|book=Life Day Treasury}}</ref>

===Arson and arenas===
{{Quote|We closed up the den and set it alight. We returned its horrors to the ''loam''. The fires reached up to the highest clouds, as Wisties danced in the embers.|Wicket Wystri Warrick|<ref name="Ewoks4">[[Ewoks (2024) 4|''Ewoks'' (2024) 4]]</ref>}}
[[File:BurningCache-2024Ewoks4.png|thumb|right|300px|Wisties danced in the embers of an Imperial weapons cache burnt by Ewoks.]]
Shortly after the Battle of Endor, a group of Imperials returned to Endor in order to [[Mission to Endor (weapons depot)|reclaim]] an [[Imperial weapons cache]] on the moon; however, it had been turned into a den by the [[Gorax]] known as the [[Great Devourer]]. The Imperials [[Death|slew]] the Great Devourer but were themselves bested by Warrick and his allies and forced to leave empty handed. Warrick and the Ewoks [[Asha Fahn]] and [[Meedro]] then discussed what should be done with the cache, which contained various vehicles, and ultimately decided to seal the den and burn it. The fire created a tall column of smoke and Wisties came to dance in the cache's embers, which Warrick told his [[Gender|brother]] [[Widdle Warrick]] about afterwards.<ref name="Ewoks4" />

In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{HuntersDate}}</ref> the Ewok [[Pilbush]] used hand-crafted capsules of Wisties as weapons while operating as a [[Hunter]] at the [[Grand Arena]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] planet [[Vespaara]].<ref name="SWH">''[[Star Wars: Hunters]]''</ref> Having looked up to the Ewoks who fought against the Empire during the [[Galactic Civil War]],<ref name="Cute But Dangerous">{{Hunters|url=news/cute-but-dangerous|text=Cute, But Dangerous!}}</ref> who used Wisties in combat,<ref name="BF II" />&mdash; Pilbush thoroughly enjoyed fighting with explosives such as Wistie capsules.<ref name="Cute But Dangerous" />

==Behind the scenes==
===Milestones===
[[File:PilbushWistieThrow-SWH.gif|thumb|right|250px|Pilbush throws a Wistie capsule in ''Star Wars: Hunters'']]
Wisties were first mentioned in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the "[[Guide to the Galaxy]]" section of the ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine's [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 38|thirty-eighth issue]], published by [[De Agostini]]<ref name="BMF 38" /> around [[September 23]], [[2015]],<ref name="BMF date">{{BMFdates|38}}</ref> and written by [[Mark Newbold]].<ref name="SM">{{DMCite|dm=File:MarkNewbold-CreditsBMF.png|creator=Mark Newbold}}</ref> The creatures later made their first canonical appearance in ''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''{{'s}} "[[W:c:battlefront:Ewok Hunt|Ewok Hunt]]" [[Star Wars video games|game]] mode,<ref name="BF II" /> released on [[April 18]], [[2018]].<ref name="SWYBY">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> They were originally introduced in the [[1984]] made-for-TV movie ''[[Caravan of Courage: An Ewok Adventure]]'',<ref name="Caravan">''[[Caravan of Courage: An Ewok Adventure]]''</ref> which is now considered a part of the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity.<ref name="SWYBY" />

In the video game ''[[Star Wars: Hunters]]'', the Wistie made its appearance following the release of Pilbush as one of the playable characters to the game<ref name="Cute But Dangerous" /> on [[September 24]], [[2024]]<ref name="S3 Patch">{{Hunters|url=news/pilbush-arrives-in-season-3-echoes-of-the-rebellion|text=Pilbush Arrives in Season 3: Echoes of the Rebellion}}</ref> and was available until the game's closure on [[October 1]], [[2025]].<ref name="HuntersClosure">{{Hunters|url=news/sunset-on-vespaara|text=Sunset on Vespaara}}</ref> The species is part of the Ewok's ability kit, which is a throwable Wistie capsule that grants opponents both slowness and damage over time when standing on the [[Wikipedia:Glossary of video game terms#area of effect|area of effect]].<ref name="SWH" />

===''Star Wars Battlefront II''===
{{Quote|I wanted the Ewoks to have a ranged, non-lethal way to damage and disperse a group of enemies. I asked Lucasfilm if we could have something made by the shaman, like a pouch of herbs or powder. ''[Lucasfilm's suggestion to include Wisties instead]'' was a perfect fit, so a lot of credit to the team at Lucasfilm for solving that gameplay need.|Manuel Llanes, game design director at [[Electronic Arts|EA]] [[DICE]]|<ref name="EA Ewok Hunt">{{EA|url=games/starwars/battlefront/star-wars-battlefront-2/news/creation-of-ewok-hunt|text=On the Creation of Ewok Hunt in Star Wars™ Battlefront™ II|author=[[Daniel Steinholtz|Steinholtz, Daniel]]|date=2018-05-24}}</ref>}}
[[File:FirefolkAttack.png|thumb|left|225px|Imperial stormtroopers under attack by Wisties in ''Star Wars Battlefront II'']]
The suggestion to include Wisties in ''Star Wars Battlefront II'' came from [[Lucasfilm]] in order to solve the gameplay need for [[W:c:battlefront:Ewok|Ewok]] abilities, which was originally considered to be a pouch of [[Plant|herbs]] or powder made by the shaman.<ref name="EA Ewok Hunt" /> The game mode depicts stormtroopers being hunted by Ewoks in the Endor forests on the [[Local day|night]] after the Battle of Endor, trying to survive until their extraction by an [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|Imperial shuttle]].<ref name="BF II" />

The ability to throw Wistie pouches was also made available for the "[[W:c:battlefront:Ewok Hunter|Ewok Hunter]]," a [[W:c:battlefront:Reinforcement|reinforcement]] unit for the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]], which was added to the game with a later update. ''Star Wars Battlefront II'' additionally features in-game challenges called "Thleek siz" and "Firefolk attack," which require throwing fifteen Wistie pouches as an Ewok and defeating fifty enemies using Wistie pouches, respectively.<ref name="BF II" /> According to the Legends [[2001]] reference book [[Galactic Phrase Book & Travel Guide (real-life book)|''Galactic Phrase Book & Travel Guide'']], the name for the former challenge means "Throw fire" in [[Ewokese]].<ref name="Phrase Book">[[Galactic Phrase Book & Travel Guide (real-life book)|''Galactic Phrase Book & Travel Guide'']]</ref>

